        "pc_requirements": {
          "minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS *:</strong> Windows 7/8/10 (any version where bunnies can flop and hop freely)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i3 2.0 GHz or AMD equivalent (or any chip that doesn’t fall asleep mid-hop)<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 1 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> AMD Radeon R3 Graphics (may not paint carrots in 4K, but it works).<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 300 MB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Without it, you’ll only see carrots, not feel them.<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Game may cause excessive squeaking and hopping around your room</li></ul>",
          "recommended": "<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 or newer (burrow-friendly) <br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Something faster than a bunny dash.<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 1 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> A card powerful enough to draw fluffy ears in HD.<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 300 MB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sound Card:</strong> Mandatory, because silence makes the bunny nervous.<br></li><li><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Game optimized for tiny bunny brain capacity</li></ul>"
        },
